{"title":"Career Roadmap · RAN Engineer","role":"RAN Engineer","summary":"A Radio Access Network (RAN) Engineer designs, deploys, integrates, configures, monitors and optimizes the part of a mobile network that connects user devices to the telecom core.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Telecommunication / Wireless (5G/6G) Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Radio Access Network (RAN) Engineer designs, deploys, integrates, configures, monitors and optimizes the part of a mobile network that connects user devices to the telecom core."},{"type":"p","text":"The RAN sits between the user equipment and the core network:"},{"type":"flow","items":["User Equipment","Radio Interface","5G RAN","Transport Network","5G Core","Internet / Enterprise Services"]},{"type":"p","text":"A RAN Engineer works primarily with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"4G LTE"},{"text":"5G NR"},{"text":"gNB"},{"text":"eNB"},{"text":"RU"},{"text":"DU"},{"text":"CU"},{"text":"RF planning"},{"text":"RF optimization"},{"text":"Antennas"},{"text":"MIMO"},{"text":"Beamforming"},{"text":"Mobility and handover"},{"text":"RAN performance"},{"text":"Network integration"},{"text":"Network troubleshooting"},{"text":"Open RAN"},{"text":"Cloud RAN"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["5G NR","RAN Architecture","RF Engineering","Network Optimization","IP/Transport","Automation","Cloud-Native RAN"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech / B.E. Telecom / Wireless","Signals + Communication + RF","Wireless Propagation + Antennas","LTE Architecture","5G NR Architecture","RAN / gNB / RU-DU-CU","RF Planning + Optimization","RAN Integration + Troubleshooting","Telecom Internship","Junior RAN Engineer","RAN Engineer","Senior RAN Engineer","RAN Optimization / Integration Specialist","RAN Architect"]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Horizon","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Electronics, signals and communication"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"RF, wireless propagation and networking"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"LTE, 5G NR and RAN architecture"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"RF planning, optimization, integration and automation"}],[{"text":"0–2 Years"},{"text":"RAN Engineer / RF Engineer"}],[{"text":"2–5 Years"},{"text":"Senior RAN / Optimization Engineer"}],[{"text":"5+ Years"},{"text":"RAN Specialist / Technical Lead"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"RAN Architect / Wireless Systems Architect"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Tech / B.E.","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Communication Engineering Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Engineering Mathematics"},{"type":"p","text":"Build proficiency in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Calculus"},{"text":"Differential equations"},{"text":"Linear algebra"},{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Complex numbers"}]},{"type":"p","text":"These are essential for signal processing and wireless communication."},{"type":"h","text":"Electrical & Electronics"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Circuit analysis"},{"text":"Analog electronics"},{"text":"Digital electronics"},{"text":"Semiconductor fundamentals"},{"text":"Filters"},{"text":"Amplifiers"},{"text":"Oscillators"},{"text":"Power electronics fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Signals & Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Continuous and discrete signals"},{"text":"LTI systems"},{"text":"Convolution"},{"text":"Fourier series"},{"text":"Fourier transform"},{"text":"Laplace transform"},{"text":"Z-transform"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Frequency-domain analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A RAN engineer needs to understand how signals behave before they can understand wireless networks."},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Communication"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ASK"},{"text":"FSK"},{"text":"PSK"},{"text":"QPSK"},{"text":"QAM"},{"text":"OFDM"},{"text":"Channel coding"},{"text":"Error correction"},{"text":"Bit error rate"},{"text":"Signal-to-noise ratio"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the relationship between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Data","Encoding","Modulation","Radio Transmission","Wireless Channel","Demodulation","Decoding","Data"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — RF & Wireless Fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"RF Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop strong knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Frequency"},{"text":"Wavelength"},{"text":"Power"},{"text":"Gain"},{"text":"dB"},{"text":"dBm"},{"text":"EIRP"},{"text":"Noise"},{"text":"Interference"},{"text":"Link budget"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to calculate basic radio link budgets."},{"type":"h","text":"Wireless Propagation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Free-space path loss"},{"text":"Reflection"},{"text":"Diffraction"},{"text":"Scattering"},{"text":"Multipath"},{"text":"Shadowing"},{"text":"Fading"},{"text":"Doppler effect"},{"text":"Penetration loss"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand why network performance varies by:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Distance"},{"text":"Frequency"},{"text":"Terrain"},{"text":"Buildings"},{"text":"Vegetation"},{"text":"User mobility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Antennas"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiation patterns"},{"text":"Gain"},{"text":"Beamwidth"},{"text":"Polarization"},{"text":"Antenna arrays"},{"text":"Sector antennas"},{"text":"Massive MIMO"},{"text":"Beamforming"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the relationship between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Antenna","Coverage","Signal Strength","Signal Quality","User Experience"]},{"type":"h","text":"MIMO"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","item